.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_solver_report" "fuzzygene_solver_report"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_solver_report \- Solver diagnostics of one virtual perturbation (exit reason, residuals, saturation).
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_solver_report(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBgene\fR as string, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockout", 
\fBsteps\fR as integer = 0, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Solver diagnostics of one virtual perturbation (exit reason, residuals, saturation).
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained (or restored) model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgene\fB \fR\- the target gene of the virtual perturbation. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR (default), \fBknockdown\fR or \fBoverexpression\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsteps\fB \fR\- maximum iteration steps; 0 uses the model configuration. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a one row data.frame
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
One row with both the mutant and the wildtype run:
 \fBexit_reason\fR / \fBiterations\fR / \fBfree_residual\fR / \fBclamp_residual\fR /
 \fBout_of_support\fR / \fBpinned\fR / \fBattractor_period\fR / \fBomega\fR / \fBtolerance\fR /
 \fBlagged\fR / \fBelapsed_ms\fR, plus the same fields prefixed with \fBcontrol_\fR.
 


 


 Read \fBexit_reason\fR first. Only \fBConverged\fR means the flat tail of the curve is a real
 steady state; \fBMaxIterations\fR is a truncated plateau, \fBLimitCycle\fR means the system
 oscillates (the period mean is the honest answer), \fBSupportSaturated\fR means the support
 clamp, not the model, produced the numbers, and \fBDiverged\fR means there is no answer.
 \fBclamp_residual\fR is a diagnostic only: the clamped gene is by construction not at a fixed
 point of the map, so it never goes to zero and must not be used as a convergence test.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
